From a99d82da2b9a9321a05a6b5f8893a338f311816b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:06:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] drm/histb: add the VDP v4 display engine

The mv200 generation uses a v4 display engine with a new register file.
Add the driver that drives its GP0 graphics path over the selected
channel, registered with the shared VDP core, and wire the standard
plane alpha property to the mixer's opacity field.

The mv310 part names its VDP words differently from the mv200 header, so
its register file is described and the GP0 fetch path is brought up on
it.

DHD0_PWR holds VPW in eight bits while the porch fields are sixteen, so
timings whose fields do not fit are rejected instead of truncated, and
the flip event is armed on the vblank -- the VDP latches the whole frame
at once -- rather than sent at once.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/histb/Kconfig           |    8 +-
 drivers/gpu/drm/histb/Makefile          |    2 +-
 drivers/gpu/drm/histb/histb-vdp-core.c  |    2 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/histb/histb-vdp.h       |    1 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/histb/histb-vdp4-regs.h |  366 ++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/histb/histb-vdp4.c      | 1117 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 1492 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/histb/histb-vdp4-regs.h
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/histb/histb-vdp4.c

